  (text "Chain: J101 BAT+ (solder pad 1; two wires from a chassis-mounted XT30, + = pin 1) -> F101 2 A 63 V fast fuse -> VBAT_FUSED -> D101 SS110 series Schottky (reverse polarity, 100 V) -> VIN_PROT:\nD102 SMAJ33A TVS + C101 22 uF/100 V electrolytic (damping) + C102 10 uF/100 V + C103 100 nF/100 V -> U101.\nOwner decision Q1: systems up to 24 V nominal (31 V equalisation). Documented alternate for 48 V only (not built): SMAJ58A/SMAJ64A, a 125 V fuse, 100 V switch MOSFETs.\nQ10: battery leads with alligator clips plug into the chassis XT30 (soldered to J101 pads, 2026-10-15); hot-plug and reversed clips are expected: D101 blocks reversal, D102/C101 handle hot-plug ringing.\nSense tap: VBAT_FUSED (after F101, ahead of D101; Kelvin track from the F101 pad) feeds the always-on divider on 03-sense; the D101 drop never enters the ADS1115 reading.\nVIN_PROT (after D101, reverse-safe) feeds the LED voltmeter switch on 05-io (W23, 2026-10-15).\nU101 LMR38010SDDAR (PFM + spread spectrum; FDDAR/FSDDAR are forced-PWM): VIN 4.2-80 V (85 V abs), 1 A; EN tied to VIN; RT 68k (E24) = 388 kHz, full regulation to 65 V;\nL101 22 uH; FB 510k/220k (E24) -> 3.318 V, no CFF; PG not used. No 5 V rail. Test points: TP102 +3V3, TP103 GND."
